# Phase 8 -- polish layer on top of Phase 7.
#
# This file is OPTIONAL and deliberately near-empty. app.py loads it
# first, then phaseSeven/orchestrator.py's own load_dotenv() fills in
# everything Phase 8 doesn't override -- so API keys (DEEPSEEK_API_KEY,
# TAVILY_API_KEY), CONFIRM_PASSWORD, and all the audio/wake tuning stay
# in phaseSeven/.env where they already are and where they are already
# working. Setting a variable here overrides phaseSeven's value for it;
# leaving it out inherits.
#
# Copy to .env only if you actually want to change one of the below.

# --- Phase 8 milestone 1: accuracy layer ---------------------------
# Timeout for the outbound HTTP calls made by the Phase 8 tools
# (Open-Meteo geocode + forecast, Tavily search).
# HTTP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=12

# How many web-search results search_web asks Tavily for. Phase 4's
# version was hardcoded to 3; the default here is deliberately higher,
# since thin result sets are one of the ways a spoken answer ends up
# confidently wrong.
# SEARCH_MAX_RESULTS=10

# How much of each result's text is kept. Phase 4 truncated to 300
# characters, which routinely cut a snippet off mid-fact.
# SEARCH_SNIPPET_CHARS=600

# --- Phase 8 milestone 2: tool expansion ---------------------------
# Wall-clock budget for find_files. It runs mid-voice-turn with a
# person waiting, so it reports stopping early rather than hanging.
# FIND_TIME_BUDGET_SECONDS=60

# Truncation limit for read_document (PDF/docx).
# DOCUMENT_MAX_CHARS=30000

# --- Phase 8 milestone 3: barge-in ---------------------------------
# Set false to restore Phase 7's plain, uninterruptible speech exactly.
# The first thing to turn off if speech ever misbehaves.
# BARGE_IN_ENABLED=true

# THE MAIN KNOB. How much louder than normal speech detection an
# utterance must be to be considered a possible interrupt. Exists
# because the mic hears Jarvis's own voice through the speakers --
# measured on a headset, a 12-second reply still produced 7 echo events
# loud enough to reach transcription (all correctly rejected, because
# detection also requires the actual word). On open speakers rather
# than a headset, this will likely need raising.
#   Jarvis interrupts itself  -> raise it
#   Saying "skip" does nothing -> lower it
# INTERRUPT_THRESHOLD_MULTIPLIER=2.5

# Replies shorter than this are spoken without starting a listener at
# all -- a four-word confirmation is over before anyone could react.
# BARGE_IN_MIN_CHARS=80

# Longest transcript still eligible to count as an interrupt. This is
# what stops Jarvis saying "I'll skip that step" from interrupting
# itself: a whole sentence is too many words to be a deliberate "skip".
# INTERRUPT_MAX_WORDS=4

# Long sentences get split further (on commas/semicolons) so one
# run-on sentence can't block interruption for fifteen seconds.
# MAX_CHUNK_CHARS=220
